# =============================================================================
# MAGIK .gitignore
#
# Rule of thumb: source code, config, and documentation are TRACKED.
# Anything regenerable, environment-specific, secret, or user/runtime data
# is IGNORED. See section headers below for the reasoning on each group.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets & environment
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.magik_test_tenants.json
deploy/aws/.secrets.local.env

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folders tracked as structure only — the directory ships via .gitkeep, but
# its contents (corpus files, user uploads, generated indexes, run logs, and
# ad-hoc scripts) are local/regenerable and stay out of git.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# docs/ IS tracked (2026-08-29). It was under the blanket rule above on the
# theory that docs are regenerable, which they are not: docs/runbooks/ holds
# the CI/CD, GPU-memory, AWS-deployment and monitoring runbooks, and
# docs/EVAL_*.md hold the per-modality accuracy write-ups. None of that can be
# regenerated from the code, and every one of them is referenced BY the code
# and by CI — cd.yml, tier2-eval.yml and quality-report.yml all send readers to
# docs/runbooks/ci-cd.md by path. An error message pointing at a file that only
# exists on the author's laptop is worse than no error message, and the same
# blanket rule already cost us exactly that once with
# scripts/generate_quality_badges.py (see its negation below).
#
# These are public-repo docs: they are prose and workflow explanations, and
# they name secrets only as NAMES (QDRANT_API_KEY, SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, ...),
# never values — verified with `detect-secrets scan docs/` before un-ignoring.
# Keep it that way; real values belong in SSM and repo secrets.

logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

scripts/*
!scripts/.gitkeep
# Tracked despite the blanket scripts/* above: quality-report.yml's `badges`
# job runs this on every manual quality run. It was never carved out, so the
# file existed only on the author's machine and the "Regenerate quality badges"
# step died with "No such file or directory" on every run that reached it —
# confirmed 2026-08-23, CD run 32633959840, under the cd.yml job this workflow
# has since replaced. Anything else added under scripts/ that CI invokes needs
# the same explicit negation here.
!scripts/generate_quality_badges.py

mlruns/
# MLflow's sqlite tracking backend (see app/eval/tracking/mlflow_logger.py —
# the old mlruns/ file backend is end-of-life and now raises rather than warns).
mlruns.db

*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python — byte-compiled files, packaging, caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so

build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.py.cover
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
cover/

.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/
cython_debug/
.ruff_cache/

# Jupyter / IPython
.ipynb_checkpoints
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
rag_env/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ML model caches & local weights — large, regenerable via download script
# (see app/bin/models/download_all_models.py)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.hf_cache/
.torch_cache/
.cuda_compat/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / frontend (ui/)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / IDEs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore
.spyderproject
.spyproject
.ropeproject
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS files
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code project state — kept local, not shared via git
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated security/supply-chain artifacts (`make sbom`, `make security-scan`)
# Regenerated on demand and per-environment — CI publishes the authoritative
# ones as workflow artifacts (see .github/workflows/cd.yml + security.yml).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
sbom.local.json
sbom.spdx.json
trivy-results.sarif
bandit-report.json
pip-audit-report.json
licenses-report.json

# Quality & Performance Reporting — quality-reports/ itself IS tracked (see
# quality-reports/README.md), but raw/noisy per-run tool output within it is
# regenerable and stays local, same principle as the bandit/pip-audit files
# above. Only the curated *.md + *.json snapshots you deliberately commit
# should land in git.
quality-reports/**/.lhci/
quality-reports/**/*-raw.xml
quality-reports/**/*-raw.json
# NOTE: quality-badges/ is deliberately NOT ignored — shields.io "endpoint"
# badges (see scripts/generate_quality_badges.py) fetch this JSON straight
# from raw.githubusercontent.com, which only serves committed files.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc tooling
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pypirc
*.exe

